1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,760
A listing searches your database by default.

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:07,844
This video shows how to turn on a product search feature, create the

3
00:00:07,844 --> 00:00:11,100
index, choose it on a listing, and what visitors see.

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,098
By default, a listing searches your database.

5
00:00:19,098 --> 00:00:22,230
For most catalogs, that is exactly right.

6
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:27,440
A large catalog, or one where the best match should come first, can

7
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,700
search a search server instead.

8
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:34,771
The visitors see the same filters, counts, sorts and pages.

9
00:00:34,771 --> 00:00:39,623
Keyword search matches the start of words, such as fo for Ford, and

10
00:00:39,623 --> 00:00:41,950
ranks the best matches first.

11
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:45,453
Turning on a search feature is not enough.

12
00:00:45,453 --> 00:00:49,010
You also create the index, and choose it on the listing.

13
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:56,335
First, turn on a product search feature:

14
00:00:56,335 --> 00:00:59,527
Elasticsearch, Lucene or Azure AI Search.

15
00:00:59,527 --> 00:01:04,350
Lucene keeps its index on your own server and needs nothing else.

16
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:09,327
Second, under Search, Indexes, add a products index, and save.

17
00:01:09,327 --> 00:01:12,560
It fills with your products in the background.

18
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:18,370
Third, edit a listing, pick the index under Search index, and publish.

19
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:24,380
Elasticsearch and Azure AI Search need their connection set up first.

20
00:01:28,584 --> 00:01:32,367
Open Tools, Features, and search for Product Search.

21
00:01:32,367 --> 00:01:35,629
Click Enable next to Product Search, Lucene.

22
00:01:35,629 --> 00:01:38,304
Lucene itself is turned on with it.

23
00:01:42,499 --> 00:01:44,396
Open Search, Indexes.

24
00:01:44,396 --> 00:01:47,349
Next to Products, Lucene, click Add.

25
00:01:49,049 --> 00:01:51,805
Enter a name for the index, and click Save.

26
00:01:51,805 --> 00:01:56,869
The index fills with your products in the background, and the list shows its status.

27
00:02:01,052 --> 00:02:04,616
Open Commerce, Product Listings, and edit the listing.

28
00:02:04,616 --> 00:02:09,309
Under Search index, which is shown once an index exists, choose the index

29
00:02:09,309 --> 00:02:11,864
you created, instead of the database.

30
00:02:11,864 --> 00:02:13,052
Click Publish.

31
00:02:17,252 --> 00:02:19,972
On the shop, visitors search as before.

32
00:02:19,972 --> 00:02:24,262
Type the start of a word, and the listing shows the products that

33
00:02:24,262 --> 00:02:27,042
match, with the same filters and counts.

34
00:02:27,494 --> 00:02:31,633
Each change to a product reaches the index when it is published, and

35
00:02:31,633 --> 00:02:36,274
the index rebuilds itself when you change your product types or their fields.

36
00:02:40,474 --> 00:02:45,716
If the search server cannot be reached, the listing searches the database instead,

37
00:02:45,716 --> 00:02:47,264
so it keeps working.

38
00:02:48,014 --> 00:02:54,565
Elasticsearch and Azure AI Search work the same way, with Products, Elasticsearch and

39
00:02:54,565 --> 00:02:57,444
Products, Azure AI Search indexes.

40
00:02:58,194 --> 00:03:02,985
The listing's keyword search can be turned off, and a listing with no

41
00:03:02,985 --> 00:03:06,114
filters and no search has no filters panel.

42
00:03:06,864 --> 00:03:10,132
A search index is not needed for a small shop.

43
00:03:10,132 --> 00:03:14,594
Add one when the database search is slow, or the ranking matters.

44
00:03:18,794 --> 00:03:20,411
A large catalog:

45
00:03:20,411 --> 00:03:22,174
search stays fast.

46
00:03:22,924 --> 00:03:26,184
A shop where the best match should come first.

47
00:03:26,934 --> 00:03:31,444
A site that already runs Elasticsearch or Azure AI Search.

48
00:03:32,194 --> 00:03:33,361
A small shop:

49
00:03:33,361 --> 00:03:34,834
keep the database.

50
00:03:36,834 --> 00:03:40,830
Turn on the feature, create the index, and choose it on the listing.

51
00:03:40,830 --> 00:03:42,234
Thanks for watching.

